   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is the bottling stage where the beer is but into bottles. Beer is a very volitile product and must be handled with care the preserve its freshness and carbonation. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The style of the bottle is also very important in preserving a beers aroma and flavor. If sunlight interacts with the beer for even as little as 10 seconds, skunking can occur, which causes the beer to produce an unpleasent aroma and changes the flavor profile. Due to this, most beer is bottled in brown glass to block sunlight. Certain beers may skunk their beers by bottling them in different color glass, such as the green bottle of Heineken.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Cans are becoming popular among many breweries due to their light blocking abilties, which is why an increase of canned beer can be seen in the market.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
